WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.362
On this slide, we are focusing on the if statement runs only when true.

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:09.382
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.382 --> 00:00:15.842
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.842 --> 00:00:19.767
An if statement runs a block only when its condition is true.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:27.517
Indentation is part of the structure, so the indented lines are the lines controlled by the decision.

00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:32.962
In real analytics, this pattern can support thresholds, validation rules, category assignment, alerts,

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:35.987
and repeated processing.

00:00:35.987 --> 00:00:41.777
The examples are intentionally small so you can trace the logic from the condition to the result.
